# .vercelignore applies repo-wide, to EVERY Vercel project connected to this
# repo — NOT scoped to a project's configured Root Directory. Earlier this
# listed "public-viewer" to keep its source out of the marketing site's
# static deploy, but that same rule was silently deleting public-viewer's
# own package.json before ITS project's build ever ran (its Root Directory
# is public-viewer, but ignore-file stripping happens on the full clone
# first) — every "npm error enoent ... public-viewer/package.json" failure
# traced back to this one line. Removed; the marketing site now just ships
# public-viewer's source as inert static files (harmless — same content is
# already public on GitHub, nothing there is executed or routed to).
downloads/README.txt
